{"id":"resp_bb21afc08470cc94","created_at":1795544539,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_88bc758fda7176a1","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to repair previous candidate SHACL based on findings. The issues:\n\n1. ADMISSION_SCOPE_ERROR: \"Other target classes select beyond declared population\". The shape currently targets nltl:ship but also other targetClasses: hullBoundaryPoint and qudt:QuantityValue. The admission specifies owner_class https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship. The population is all ships; other target classes beyond population cause error. We need to constrain activation so shapes only apply within population boundary. Usually we can use sh:targetClass only for ship, and use sh:property to enforce constraints on related nodes, but not target them as separate shapes? The HullBoundaryShape and ShellAngleQuantityShape target classes hullBoundaryPoint and qudt:QuantityValue, which is beyond declared population. To fix, we should remove sh:targetClass from those secondary shapes and instead use sh:node constraint within property of ShipBoundaryShape, and perhaps use sh:property with sh:node to validate nested structures but not target them globally. So we can keep hullBoundary shape as a node shape without a targetClass, referenced via sh:node. Similarly for quantity shape. Then activation will be only for hullBoundaryPoint nodes reachable from ship via property.\n\nThus modify:\n\n- ShipBoundaryShape: keep as is (targetClass nltl:ship)\n- HullBoundaryShape: remove sh:targetClass line; keep as shape for validation of hullBoundaryPoint but not globally targeted.\n- ShellAngleQuantityShape: remove sh:targetClass qudt:QuantityValue.\n\nAlso adjust the paths: The property in HullBoundaryShape uses sh:path nltl:shellInclinationAngle; that's fine.\n\nAdditionally canonical identifier errors: using qudt:numericValue and qudt:unit identifier need to be corrected to full IRIs http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue (current uses qudt:numericValue prefix mapping? In previous candidate, they used sh:path qudt:numericValue; but the prefix qudt: is declared as <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt#>. However the correct identifier is http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue (i.e., not #). The schema defines numericValue IRI without fragment? Actually declared in JSON-LD mapping: \"numericValue\": { \"@id\": \"qudt:numericValue\", ... } where prefix qudt: is http://qudt.org/schema/qudt# . So qudt:numericValue expands to ...#numericValue, which is not the canonical IRI (they expect no #). Therefore need to replace usage with full IRI http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue (and similarly for unit). In SHACL, we can use the full IRI directly or define a prefix for that base. Since existing prefix qudt points to ...# we cannot use that; we can define another prefix, e.g., qdt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> (without #). Or we can use the full IRI in the path. Simpler: replace sh:path qudt:numericValue with the full IRI IRI in angle brackets. Same for unit.\n\nSimilarly, targetClass for quantity shape currently qudt:QuantityValue expands to ...#QuantityValue, need replace with full IRI http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/QuantityValue.\n\nThus repair:\n\n- In ShellAngleQuantityShape, change sh:targetClass to the full IRI (or remove targetClass entirely as we will not target globally). Probably we remove it.\n\nBut we still need shape to apply to those QuantityValue nodes via sh:node. So shape will be used as node shape but without targetClass.\n\nHence modifications:\n\nHullBoundaryShape: no sh:targetClass; but keep as a shape.\n\nShellAngleQuantityShape: also no sh:targetClass; use exact IRIs for paths.\n\nDefine prefixes: keep existing prefixes, maybe add:\n\n@prefix qdt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\n\nAnd we can use qdt:numericValue etc. Or just use <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue>. We'll add prefix qdt for readability.\n\nAlso, need to keep numeric value as decimal 7. The numeric term review suggests maybe need numeric equality vs exact term; we keep exact literal with datatype decimal.\n\nNow ADMISSION_SCOPE_ERROR also may require adding sh:activation? Usually you can use sh:targetClass only for ship shape, that's fine.\n\nThus final SHACL:\n\n- prefixes include qdt.\n\n- ShipBoundaryShape unchanged.\n\n- HullBoundaryShape: a sh:NodeShape ; sh:property as before referencing ShellAngleQuantityShape. No sh:targetClass.\n\n- ShellAngleQuantityShape: a sh:NodeShape ; sh:property for numericValue and unit with full IRIs.\n\nWe also need to ensure sh:node constraint from HullBoundaryShape references the shape for QuantityValue.\n\nThus final block with <BEGIN_SHACL> ... <END_SHACL>.\n\nLet's construct.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_83fe6c110a93f840","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt#> .            # original (fragment) prefix – kept for compatibility\n@prefix qdt:  <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .            # canonical (no‑fragment) prefix required by the schema\n@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape that targets every ship (the admitted population) and\n# requires a single hull‑boundary point linked via\n# nltl:hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint.\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n<https://w3id.org/nltl/shapes#ShipBoundaryShape>\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n        sh:node <https://w3id.org/nltl/shapes#HullBoundaryShape> ;\n    ] .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape that validates the hull‑boundary point referenced from a ship.\n# This shape is **not** globally targeted; it is activated only when a\n# ship instance has a hasBottomRegionLowerRegionBoundaryPoint property.\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n<https://w3id.org/nltl/shapes#HullBoundaryShape>\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:shellInclinationAngle ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n        sh:node <https://w3id.org/nltl/shapes#ShellAngleQuantityShape> ;\n    ] .\n\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n# Shape that validates the QUDT QuantityValue representing the shell\n# inclination.  The shape is invoked only via the node constraint above.\n# -----------------------------------------------------------------\n<https://w3id.org/nltl/shapes#ShellAngleQuantityShape>\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qdt:numericValue ;               # canonical IRI http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/numericValue\n        sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n        sh:hasValue \"7\"^^xsd:decimal ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qdt:unit ;                       # canonical IRI http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/unit\n        sh:hasValue unit:DEG ;\n    ] .\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":23759,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":64,"cache_write_tokens":23680,"input_tokens_per_turn":[23759],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[64]},"output_tokens":1654,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":1022,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[1654],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":25413},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}